thanks to the release of the suicide  squad the villain known as bloodsport  has taken  center stage in the dc eu but just who  is this rampaging rascal and  why is he such a big deal in the world  of comics this  is the untold truth of bloodsport we're  all gonna die  i hope so oh for god's sake  the original bloodsport is robert dubois  a madman who kills  dozens of innocent metropolis citizens  during a rampage that unfolds in  superman volume 2 number 4.  dubois commands a seemingly endless  arsenal of high-tech weaponry  that he can teleport into his grasp  including a pistol that fires slivers of  kryptonite  he is portrayed as perpetually enraged  vietnam war veteran  often yelling at his victims that  they're wasting the freedom he  fought to preserve after bloodsport's  initial attack on a restaurant in which  he massacres over two dozen civilians  superman gets involved in corners dubois  in a bowling alley  bloodsport wounds superman with a  kryptonite bullet but thankfully jimmy  olsen's timely intervention  saves kalel from certain death in the  meantime the fact that bloodsport is  access to kryptonite leads superman to  correctly deduce that dubois sponsor  is none other than lex luthor it's jimmy  olsen who figures out the key to  defeating bloodsport when his research  leads him to the discovery that the  villain  never actually served in vietnam when  his number came  up he fled to canada and his younger  brother mickey went to vietnam in his  place  losing his arms and legs for his trouble  dubois's guilt  drove him mad and turned him into  bloodsport  jimmy finds mickey and brings him to the  battle where he pleads with bloodsport  to stop his rampage  bloodsport collapses in tears at the  sight of his brother and the gunman is  sent to a maximum security psychiatric  facility  of course that's not the last of  bloodsport not  by a long shot adventures of superman  number 507  opens with a heavily armed masked man  who calls himself bloodsport  interrupting a mugging in a metropolis  alleyway as he kills two of the three  muggers you may believe  he's a crime fighter with less forgiving  tactics similar to marvel's punisher  but when he cuts down the victim of the  mugging too things start to become a  little clearer  this is alex trent a white supremacist  dedicated to killing as many people of  color as he can  the story bleeds into action comics  number 694 and over the course of both  issues the new bloodsport kills even  more innocence than his predecessor  mostly people of color though he's also  happy to turn his  violent attentions to whites he despises  for consorting with other races  with the arrival of the cyborg villain  high tech it's revealed that both she  and bloodsport are pawns of the demon  blood thirst  bloodsport is presumed dead following an  explosion at the end of action comics  number 694 but  the following year in action comics  number 702  he returns to continue his racist  rampage just as jimmy olsen is key to  defeating the original bloodsport  it's another daily planet employee  reporter ron troop who locates trent's  achilles heel  like dubois before him trent teleports  his weapons to his hands though  his teleporter is implanted in his chest  so no one can take it from him  however troop tracks down bloodsport's  weapons cash and destroys it leaving  nothing for the races to fight with  superman captures trent who is  subsequently sent to stryker's island  prison  in 1995's adventures of superman number  526  robert dubois falls victim to the most  devastating villain of all  budget cuts needing to siphon off some  of its patience the psychiatric facility  where dubois is being treated has  transferred him to striker's island  prison  the same prison alex trent was said to  after his latest series of killings  dubois and trent are destined to collide  and things don't go well for  either of them hoping to ease tensions  in his prison  the striker's island warden agrees to a  boxing match between the two bloodsports  with the proviso that superman acts as a  referee the man of steel  agrees though he accurately deduces that  allowing the boxing match probably isn't  a great idea in the first place  the match itself doesn't last very long  dubois easily dominates trent in its  early stages after which trent tackles  his opponent  to the ground but when superman pulls  the boxers apart trent reveals a gun  as it turns out his aryan brotherhood  allies have managed to get him a new  cache of weapons  a riot quickly erupts and superman must  struggle to control the rampaging  prisoners while trying to get a hold of  dubois and trent  dubois manages to get trent's gun from  him and even escapes past the walls of  the prison but  he's quickly gunned down and killed by  the guards trent  survives the riot but not for long his  aryan brotherhood buddies learn that at  one point  during the chaos superman had to save  trent from dubois ashamed that a black  man got the better of trent the  brotherhood  burns trent to death in his cell the  third version of bloodsport to appear in  the comics has so far proven to be the  most  mysterious unlike the late robert dubois  and alex trent he doesn't make any claim  about twisted ideals serving as his  inspiration  and like many super villains he seems to  don his red skull cap mask  purely for the money during the late  2000s bloodsport appears as one of the  five villains hired to kill the man of  steel by the criminal organization  intergang the others being riot silver  banshee livewire and helgermite  this story is part of dc's one year  later event in which superman's powers  are just beginning to return after a  battle with superboy prime  superman's narration indicates that this  bloodsport's techniques are at least a  little different from those of his  predecessors and suggests that the  teleportation he uses to retrieve his  weapons is  extra dimensional in nature in spite of  his weakened state  superman is eventually able to defeat  the five villains  this new bloodsport's name is never  revealed but it's clear he's more of a  mercenary than the villains who  previously took the name  he expresses excitement at the money  offered for superman's life particularly  after some of his comrades have been  defeated and he realizes he could get a  bigger piece of the pie  this bloodsport's given name has yet to  be revealed and since one year later  most of his appearances have come in the  form of cameos bloodsport made his mark  on the dc  animated universe in the mid-2000s  though in a relatively  minor role in 2005 he made his first  appearance on justice league unlimited  in season 2's  the cat in the canary the episode  revolves around a metabrawl run by the  entrepreneurial villain roulette  in this epic showdown super villains and  heroes fight for sport  some of them against their will here  bloodsport is introduced  briefly as he's locking horns with the  batman bad guy electrocutioner it isn't  clear whether or not bloodsport survives  the events of justice league unlimited  though it seems unlikely while he's  usually only seen in the background  bloodsport is a member of the legion of  doom in the series but when the legion  of doom's spaceship is destroyed by  darkseid  in the show's penultimate episode it  isn't revealed whether or not  bloodsports survives  his death is implied however as he isn't  one of the villains saved by star  sapphire  and sinestro it's never really made  clear exactly  who this version of bloodsport is  supposed to be his given name isn't  revealed  and the unnamed version of bloodsport  had yet to appear in dc's comics at the  time the series was produced  for the time being this has to be  chalked up as yet another unsolved  bloodsport mystery  before idris elba took the role in the  suicide squad david st  lewis played robert dubois in the season  3 premiere of cw's supergirl  however while he shares dubois name  there are significant differences  between this bloodsport  and the villain from the source material  instead of covering up his draft dodging  like the original bloodsport  supergirl's version does have a military  background which proves invaluable in  his job as a terrorist for hire  meet robert dubois goes by bloodsport  which is  not any sport i've ever heard of  bloodsport first locks horns with  supergirl in the cold open of  girl of steel when she joins the  national city police in pursuit of  dubois and his goons  while he doesn't appear to have any  meta-human abilities bloodsport is  clearly close to peak human condition as  he not only survives getting knocked a  hundred yards through the air by  supergirl and crashing onto the roof of  a parked car  but he's even able to brush himself off  and escape moments later  it's later revealed that bloodsport is  working for the crooked businessman  morgan edge at edge's behest  bloodsport steals some captured alien  technology then uses it to cloak a  submarine  and attack the city's waterfront  inevitably however he's quickly defeated  by supergirl  and arrested robert dubois's time in the  afterlife comes to an end in 2021's  suicide squad number five the issue  opens with a quick recap of dubois  origin  though there's no mention of his death  in 1995's adventures of superman number  526  with all the various reboots and  reworkings dc's continuity has undergone  since 1995 it can  probably be assumed either that dubois  was resurrected by undisclosed means in  the intervening years  or that his death at striker's island  prison has been erased from history  bloodsport's role in the suicide squad  is more specific than the rest of task  force x  amanda waller sends him through a number  of different dimensions gathering  intel and recruiting new captives for  waller to use  to help him waller arms dubois with a  new suit and helmet to protect him from  the strains of interdimensional travel  as well as a nearly unlimited arsenal of  weapons that he can teleport to himself  across dimensions while a flashback  montage early in suicide squad number  five suggests that bloodsport has been  going at solo for a while  he probably won't be able to manage on  his own for long the issue finds him in  earth  3 the home of the crime syndicate a  group of supercrooks made up of sadistic  versions of the justice league heroes  by the end of the issue bloodsport is  captured by ultraman  earth 3's brutish answer to superman  forcing waller to send in a new team to  bring bloodsport home  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  you

